	(text "POWER (all receiver rails on one sheet)\nTopology chosen by Danilo 2026-11-19: one switcher, no linear regulators in the main path.\n5V_MAIN (5.0 V nominal, down to 3.7 V during power-fail hold-up) -> TPS62065 buck at 3.35 V -> one damped LC filter per rail.\nRX_PWR_EN from the main board enables the buck, so the power-fail signal can shed the whole receiver at once.\nEach filter: 2.2 uH into 22 uF, damped by 47 uF in series with 0.5 ohm (two 1 ohm in parallel). Simulated: about 74 dB at 2.2 MHz, 18 mV drop at 180 mA.\nParts confirmed by the sourcing thread 2026-11-19 (MPN and LCSC fields on each symbol).\nSimulation check 2026-11-19: filters about 73 dB at 3 MHz with derated capacitors; rails 3.335 to 3.345 V.\nBRING-UP CHECK: on the first RX_PWR_EN edge, scope 3.35V_RX_BUCK at J1 and 3.3V_SYNTH. The buck starts in current limit (about 141 uF to charge in a 250 us ramp);\nwith C2 at 33 pF the worst simulated peak is 3.40 V (TI model; 10 pF gave 3.50 to 3.53 V). Confirm the peak stays under 3.5 V (MAX1193 absolute maximum is 3.6 V, the tightest part; ADF4351 3.9 V, MAX2659 4.2 V, MAX2682 6.0 V, TCXO 3.6 V operating). If it overshoots: change C2 to 47 pF. Do not shrink the damper capacitors (22 uF dampers still gave 3.49 V).\nOPEN: 3 MHz harmonics 15 to 18 fall inside the IF band, so U1 and L1 go far from the IF amplifiers and converters.\nTO ADD: rail test points."
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "43e236b2-2f3d-5656-aa11-625ece5a3a42")
	)
