	(text "R10 holds the receiver off until the main board drives RX_PWR_EN.\nR11 is the link to remove for bench tests with U1 off."
		(at 35.56 139.7 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "da0f36ee-09ab-5389-9100-00c0ef63e425")
	)
	(text "Buck: 3.345 V = 0.6 V x (1 + 549k / 120k). MODE tied high for forced fixed-frequency PWM (about 3 MHz).\nDatasheet: R2 120k to 360k, R1 + R2 under about 1 Mohm. C2 is 33 pF C0G, above the datasheet formula value of 11.6 pF, to stop start-up overshoot\n(TI transient model, approved by Danilo 2026-11-20). Fallback if the scope shows more than 3.5 V: 47 pF (CL10C470JB8NNNC, C1671).\nPlace C1 at PVIN. Keep U1 and L1 away from the IF section."
		(at 35.56 96.52 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "1db1125e-a36f-53e1-b20d-efc4d7316c95")
	)
